    "explanation": "Both accounts agree on the essentials, and the records confirm them. The trip deviated 1.90 km from the recommended route (25.10 km actual minus 23.20 km recommended, EV-TRIP-06008; POL-RD-22), above the 1.0 km tolerance. The driver told you in-app before the turn — MSG-06008-003 at 18:42:36, about three minutes before the deviation was logged at 18:45:16 — giving a reason (an accident on the PIE near Bedok) and the alternative roads, and you agreed, 'ok, thanks' (MSG-06008-004); so the deviation was notified and acknowledged (POL-RD-21). The fare charged was 39.98 SGD; the deviation-related part of it is the excess distance fare, 1.90 x 0.92 = 1.75 SGD (POL-RD-24), against the 6.50 SGD the rider contests. The case turns on whether traffic justified the reroute, and that cannot be established. POL-RD-23 makes traffic data for the recommended route at the trip time the only thing that can justify a reroute, and the platform's LTA traffic-feed request for this window failed and was not retried, so EV-ADVIS-06008-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and carries no fact (POL-GEN-02). The record is silent on the PIE at that hour, and that silence is not a finding that there was no accident. The driver's 'I saw it on the map' is an assertion without data, and POL-RD-23 says an assertion alone does not justify a reroute — so the driver cannot win on his own say-so. But the rider's contrary reading fails too: POL-RD-23 shows the driver has not proved justification; it does not establish that no traffic existed. Because the traffic question is undetermined, no row of POL-RD-24 fits — row (a) needs the reroute traffic-justified and row (d) needs it not traffic-justified, and neither is shown — and POL-GEN-26 is explicit that a fact a rule needs (it names 'whether traffic justified the reroute') that cannot be established because the evidence that would carry it is missing escalates the case, with no outcome inferred from the absence. On who may decide: the contested value is 6.50 SGD (POL-GEN-22's final band), with no fraud flag, no safety flag and a 1.90 km deviation under the unapplied 2.0 km limb, but POL-RD-25 requires 0.80 confidence for a route-deviation ruling and the missing traffic artifact caps confidence at 0.0, so the AI ruling cannot stand. Outcome: ESCALATE. The 6.50 SGD is held — neither refunded to the rider nor retained by the driver — until a human reviewer resolves the traffic question; the reviewer should have the platform retry the LTA traffic-feed request for the recommended PIE segment over the trip window (2026-09-27, about 18:29-19:05). No referral applies: a route deviation has no referral clause in this version."
