    "confidence": 0.0,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. I have read the trip record, the driver's GPS trace, the in-app chat, the fare ledger and the two profile snapshots. I cannot decide the money on this record, so the case goes to a human reviewer and the fare is held rather than refunded or kept.\n\nWhat the record does establish. The recommended route was 23.20 km and the vehicle travelled 25.10 km, a deviation of 1.90 km (POL-RD-22, EV-TRIP-06008), which is above the 1.0 km tolerance. The vehicle left the PIE at the Bedok North Avenue 3 exit at 18:45:16 and rejoined at Loyang Avenue / Upper Changi Road North at 19:01:07. The driver told the rider before the deviation, by in-app chat: MSG-06008-003 at 18:42:36 ('PIE got accident near Bedok, I go New Upper Changi Road then Upper Changi Road North, ok?'), answered 'ok, thanks' at 18:43:01. POL-RD-21's notice requirement is therefore met and the reroute was agreed. These facts are carried by complete artifacts at weight 1.0, and I accept the driver's claims on them.\n\nWhat the record cannot establish. POL-RD-23 makes a reroute traffic-justified only where traffic data for the recommended route at the trip time shows congestion, an incident or a closure. The traffic advisory for this trip, EV-ADVIS-06008-01, is MISSING (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight_multiplier 0.0): the platform's request to the LTA historical traffic feed timed out and was not retried. The record is silent on whether there was an accident on the PIE near Bedok — the artifact itself records that this is not a finding that there was no traffic — and a MISSING artifact carries no fact (POL-GEN-02(3)). The driver's belief that he 'saw it on the map' is an assertion with no supporting data and, on POL-RD-23, does not justify the reroute.\n\nWhy the AI cannot rule. POL-RD-24's matrix turns on traffic justification: row (a) (no refund) needs the reroute traffic-justified; row (d) (refund of the excess distance fare) needs it not traffic-justified. Neither can be found, so no row fits, and POL-RD-24 sends a case that fits no row to escalation under POL-GEN-26 — which names 'whether traffic justified the reroute' among the facts that must be escalated when the evidence that would carry it is missing. The rider's argument that the empty record is itself proof the reroute was not justified is not accepted: silence is not a finding of no traffic, and POL-RD-23's rule about a bare assertion is not a finding about the traffic itself. An undecided limb supports neither a payment that needs the clause to hold nor a refund that needs it to fail.\n\nThe money. I accept the rider's figures — deviation 1.90 km (25.10 minus 23.20), excess distance fare 1.90 x 0.92 = 1.75 SGD (POL-RD-24, matching the ledger's excess_distance_fare_sgd), with nothing returning the base fare, the time fare of 8.64, the platform fee of 0.90 or the surge of 3.55 — but because traffic justification cannot be established I cannot award even that 1.75, and I cannot return the whole 6.50 SGD the rider asks for. The claim that the AI can decide without escalation (POL-GEN-22, POL-RD-25, POL-GEN-26) is not accepted: the fact the traffic limb turns on is carried only by a MISSING artifact of weight 0.0, so confidence is capped at 0.00 under POL-GEN-02(2), below the 0.80 POL-RD-25 requires. The amount contested, 6.50 SGD, is below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band and neither profile carries a fraud flag, but that does not cure the missing traffic record.\n\nOpen question for the reviewer: whether traffic on the PIE near Bedok around 18:45 on 27 September 2026 justified the reroute — the LTA historical traffic feed should be retried. If it did, POL-RD-24 row (a) applies (the rider was informed and agreed) and nothing is refunded; if it did not, row (d) applies and the excess distance fare of 1.75 SGD is returned. The 39.98 SGD fare is held pending that check."
